; ------------------------------------------------------
; Stat increase pointers and EXP values
; 
; Stat increase
; 
; 1 = HP
; 2 = TP 
; 3 = Damage
; 4 = Defense
; 5 = Speed
; 6 = Luck
; 7 = Skill
;
; You can easily extend EXP tables and make characters reach lv 99 if you wish.
; Keep in mind that the values for EXP are the total EXP the a character needs to learn
; and not the EXP needed to go up a level. So for a certain level, make sure you don't have values equal or less than
; the previous levels or there will most likely be bugs.
;
; Speaking of bugs, the last value of the table for EXP (the one before the 0's) will not
; count as a level up, meaning it there won't be stat increases and the game
; will not update the level counter. Remove the -1 from the count before the
; start of that table. So for example:
;
; dc.l	(RhysExpPoints_End-RhysExpPoints)/4-1
; 
; becomes
;
; dc.l	(RhysExpPoints_End-RhysExpPoints)/4
; ------------------------------------------------------
	
